.TH NERD-CHAT 1 "2026-11-09" "sine-loco 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sine-loco \- serverless chat over Tor onion services (terminal version)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sine-loco
[\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fB\-\-ram\fR] [\fB\-\-low\-mem\fR] [\fB\-\-keyfile\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-tor\-control\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Messages exist only in memory; contacts live in an encrypted vault file. Unaudited software: read SECURITY.md in /usr/share/doc/sine-loco before relying on it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-vault PATH
Vault file. Default: ~/.local/share/sine-loco/sine-loco.vault.
.TP
.B \-\-ram
RAM only: never write anything to disk.
.TP
.B \-\-low\-mem
Use the 128 MiB key\-derivation profile.
.TP
.B \-\-keyfile PATH
Second factor file (at least 32 bytes). Keep it on a separate device.
.TP
.B \-\-tor\-control ADDR
Use an already running Tor (for example Tails or Whonix) instead of starting one.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-swap
Start even if swap is active (default: refuse).
.TP
.B \-\-strip IN OUT
Clean one JPEG/PNG (add \-\-text for plain text) into a new file, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-probe\-tor
Report what the Tor on this machine allows, then exit.
.PP
Run with an unknown option to print the complete list. Press ? in the program for the key help.
.SH SEE ALSO
sine-loco-gui(1), /usr/share/doc/sine-loco/GETTING_STARTED.md
